From: losos <losos@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web_contents: Lay pages out like Chrome for Android with
 --enable-viewport

On Linux the switch turned on only the layout viewport and still ignored
the page's viewport meta tag. Turn on the rest of what Android's
WebPreferences defaults are, as DevTools' phone emulation does: the meta
tag, fit to screen, the mobile viewport style, text-size-adjust, double
tap to zoom and zooming focused fields to a legible scale.
---
 .../browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc | 22 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
index c6d3b30..db145ef 100644
--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
@@ -3981,6 +3981,28 @@ const blink::web_pref::WebPreferences WebContentsImpl::ComputeWebPreferences(
 
   prefs.viewport_enabled = command_line.HasSwitch(switches::kEnableViewport);
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+  // Uranium on a phone. Upstream, --enable-viewport turns on only the 980px
+  // layout viewport and leaves <meta name="viewport"> ignored, which reads
+  // worse on a phone than no viewport at all. The launcher passes it when
+  // every screen is phone-sized, so here it means what WebPreferences'
+  // Android defaults mean: honour the page's viewport tag, fit the page to
+  // the screen and let it zoom out to that, Android's viewport UA style,
+  // text-size-adjust, double tap to zoom, zooming a focused field up to a
+  // readable size, and a rotation that resizes the page as an orientation
+  // change. DevTools' phone emulation sets the same, so Blink already does
+  // all of it on Linux.
+  if (prefs.viewport_enabled) {
+    prefs.viewport_meta_enabled = true;
+    prefs.shrinks_viewport_contents_to_fit = true;
+    prefs.viewport_style = blink::mojom::ViewportStyle::kMobile;
+    prefs.text_size_adjust_enabled = true;
+    prefs.double_tap_to_zoom_enabled = true;
+    prefs.auto_zoom_focused_editable_to_legible_scale = true;
+    prefs.main_frame_resizes_are_orientation_changes = true;
+  }
+#endif
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
   // TODO(crbug.com/40925473): GetPrimaryDisplay() won't be correct for
   // externally connected displays. Get the display where Chrome is opened
